      "updated": 1793379157321,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Adjacency Matrix Representation\n==============================\n\n1. It is a square matrix .\n\n2. This is beacuse number of rows and number of cols are same and\nare equal to number of vertices .\n\n3. This matrix stores 1 in adj[i][j] if we have a direct path from\nvertex i to vertex j otherwise it stores 0 .",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Adjacency Matrix Representation\n==============================\n\n1. It is a square matrix .\n\n2. This is beacuse number of rows and number of cols are same and are equal to number of vertices .\n\n3. This matrix stores 1 in adj[i][j] if we have a direct path from vertex i to vertex j otherwise it stores 0 .",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
